{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Judges and officers.</b> שׁוֹפְטִים — judges who decide the law; שׁוֹטְרִים — those who drive the people after their rulings (striking and binding) with rod and strap until he accepts upon himself the judge's sentence." "<b>In all your gates.</b> In every city." "<b>For your tribes.</b> It modifies <b>you shall appoint</b> — 'judges and officers you shall appoint for your tribes in all your gates which YHWH your Elohim gives you.'" "<b>For your tribes.</b> This teaches that judges are appointed for every tribe and in every city (Sifrei; Sanhedrin 16)." "<b>And they shall judge the people, etc.</b> Appoint judges expert and righteous to judge justly (cf. Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:23.308003723Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}